.TH SDL_ClipboardDataCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_ClipboardDataCallback \- Callback function that will be called when data for the specified mime-type is requested by the OS.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_clipboard.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef const void *(SDLCALL *SDL_ClipboardDataCallback)(void *userdata, const char *mime_type, size_t *size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The callback function is called with NULL as the mime_type when the clipboard is cleared or new data is set\[char46] The clipboard is automatically cleared in
.BR SDL_Quit ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
a pointer to the provided user data\[char46]
.TP
.I mime_type
the requested mime-type\[char46]
.TP
.I size
a pointer filled in with the length of the returned data\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the data for the provided mime-type\[char46] Returning NULL or setting the length to 0 will cause zero length data to be sent to the \(dqreceiver\(dq, which should be able to handle this\[char46] The returned data will not be freed, so it needs to be retained and dealt with internally\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetClipboardData (3)
